---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout title="About - Tailspin Toys">
  <div class="py-16">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-bold bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 via-purple-400 to-blue-300 bg-clip-text text-transparent mb-6">
        About Tailspin Toys
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Where DevOps meets tabletop gaming. We're pioneering the intersection of software development culture and strategic board games.
      </p>
      <div class="w-24 h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-purple-500 mx-auto mt-8 rounded-full"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-slate-800/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-slate-700/50 rounded-2xl shadow-2xl">
        <!-- Background elements -->
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-500/5 via-purple-500/5 to-indigo-500/5"></div>
        <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-40 h-40 bg-blue-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div>
        <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-40 h-40 bg-purple-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div>

        <div class="relative p-8 sm:p-12 space-y-8">
          <!-- Mission Section -->
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6 flex items-center">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 mr-4 text-blue-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
              </svg>
              Our Mission
            </h2>
            <div class="bg-slate-800/30 backdrop-blur-sm border border-slate-700/30 rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
              <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                Tailspin Toys is the premier crowdfunding platform dedicated to bringing board games with a development and DevOps twist to life. We believe that the same collaborative spirit, iteration cycles, and problem-solving that power modern software teams can make for endlessly engaging tabletop experiences.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
              By focusing exclusively on games that explore themes like continuous integration, agile planning, container orchestration, and incident response, we offer a unique space where both seasoned developers and curious newcomers can back - and even contribute to - the games they're most passionate about.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Platform Features -->
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6 flex items-center">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 mr-4 text-purple-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19.428 15.428a2 2 0 00-1.022-.547l-2.387-.477a6 6 0 00-3.86.517l-.318.158a6 6 0 01-3.86.517L6.05 15.21a2 2 0 00-1.806.547M8 4h8l-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 00.586 1.414l5 5c1.26 1.26.367 3.414-1.415 3.414H4.828c-1.782 0-2.674-2.154-1.414-3.414l5-5A2 2 0 009 9.172V5L8 4z" />
              </svg>
              What We Offer
            </h2>
            <div class="bg-slate-800/30 backdrop-blur-sm border border-slate-700/30 rounded-xl p-6">
              <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300 mb-6">
                Our platform empowers creators at every stage of the design journey. From early-concept sketches through final prototype testing, Tailspin Toys provides tools for community feedback, stretch-goal planning, and beta-play sessions.
              </p>
              <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                Backers can join forums to share house rules, vote on art directions, or fund expansion modules that introduce new mechanics like "pipeline bottleneck" challenges or "rollback" rescue cards. We handle all the logistics of manufacturing and fulfillment, so designers can focus on the fun stuff - and supporters can look forward to high-quality components delivered right to their door.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Our Story -->
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6 flex items-center">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 mr-4 text-indigo-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.746 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.246 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253" />
              </svg>
              Our Story
            </h2>
            <div class="bg-slate-800/30 backdrop-blur-sm border border-slate-700/30 rounded-xl p-6">
              <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
                The name "Tailspin Toys" reflects our love of both flight metaphors and that moment when a project takes on a life of its own - spinning through sprints, releases, and hotfixes until it soars. Founded by a team of developers who were always gamers at heart, we know firsthand how satisfying it is to conquer a tricky bug or pull off a flawless deployment - and how much more rewarding it can be to beat your friends on a table (or work with them cooperatively to win together).
              </p>
              <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300 mt-4">
                Whether you're here to back your next favorite game or to launch your own DevOps-inspired design, welcome aboard. Let's game from here, together!
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Features Grid -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-12">
            <div class="text-center group">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-500/20 to-blue-600/20 border border-blue-500/30 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-blue-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm6 3a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zM7 10a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0z" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Community-Driven</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Built by developers, for developers and game enthusiasts</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-center group">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-purple-500/20 to-purple-600/20 border border-purple-500/30 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-purple-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4M7.835 4.697a3.42 3.42 0 001.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 014.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 001.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 013.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010 4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-4.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138-3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010-4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 013.138-3.138z" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Quality Assured</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Every game goes through rigorous testing and review</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-center group">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-500/20 to-indigo-600/20 border border-indigo-500/30 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-indigo-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-2">Innovation First</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Cutting-edge gameplay that mirrors modern DevOps practices</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Back to Games CTA -->
      <div class="text-center mt-12">
        <a 
          href="/" 
          class="group inline-flex items-center bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-purple-600 hover:from-blue-500 hover:to-purple-500 text-white font-semibold py-4 px-8 rounded-xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-blue-500/25 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:scale-105"
        >
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mr-3 transform transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-1" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M9.707 14.707a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 010-1.414l4-4a1 1 0 011.414 1.414L7.414 9H15a1 1 0 110 2H7.414l2.293 2.293a1 1 0 010 1.414z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
          <span>Back to Games</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>